Original repository path: VERIFICATION_MATRIX.md

# Tiny Image Star verification contract

The immediate regression command is:

```bash
npm run verify
```

The equivalent contributor entry point is `make verify`; Make delegates to the
same npm scripts and also exposes the Pages artifact checks.

It is dependency-light, returns nonzero on failure, and exercises the copied
fixture through the actual Pillow-RS adapter path. It checks transformed PNG
bytes, decoded dimensions, exact crop/rotate/flip pixel rows, all eight EXIF
orientations, indexed PNG, corrupt/truncated rejection, output-size rejection,
unsupported-format rejection, real fixed-setting JPEG output and alpha
flattening, preset data, fresh editor state, module composition,
readiness/progress separation, worker revision/cancellation wiring, batch
selection wiring, input safety/duplicate handling, exact batch byte-limit
boundaries, pixel-aware worker scheduling, and the 100,000-entry metadata-only
folder-job contract.

The local save watcher reruns that same fast command after a 250 ms debounce:

```bash
npm run verify:watch
```

This is an opt-in local command, not a scheduled job or hook. It watches the
current source and test files with low-overhead polling. GitHub Actions runs
the complete `npm run verify:all` gate for pull requests and before Pages
deployment from `main`.

The slower browser interaction layer is separate from the save watcher:

```bash
npm run verify:browser
```

It drives the static app with the Playwright development dependency declared
in `package.json` and returns `2` with an install message if dependencies are
not installed. It checks actual page state, worker-backed previews,
interaction transitions, and console errors; it is intentionally not part of
the save watcher.

For a complete local/CI gate after `npm ci`, run:

```bash
npm run verify:all
```

This combines the real-byte contract and browser smoke. It is expected to
fail rather than silently skip the browser half when Playwright is absent.

## Feature matrix

`A` is covered by `npm run verify`; `B` is covered by the separate headless
browser smoke; `M` is the equivalent in-app browser check when a headless
browser cannot be launched.

The gate validates behavior and real output bytes. The project does not
currently produce a line/branch coverage artifact, so a passing run is not a
line-coverage percentage claim.

The full gate also runs `npm run check:docs`, which validates repository-local
Markdown targets. External URL availability and anchor semantics remain a
manual/release-review boundary.

| User-visible feature | Check | Evidence / boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Fresh Ready state | A + B/M | Worker reaches the internal `Ready` state; the healthy badge stays hidden in the empty UI and processing text is separate. |
| Calm empty editor and contextual workspace navigation | B/M | Browser verifies empty state hides disabled tool panels, hides stale activity/comparison controls, offers both Choose images and Choose a folder, routes one-file and multi-file imports through the same canvas/tray workspace, labels the active-set action `Results (N)`, and returns through `Back to editor`. It also proves the old competing Canvas and Return-to-set controls are absent. |
| File import | A + B/M | Deterministic PNG, JPEG, BMP, WebP, GIF, TIFF, ICO, indexed PNG, and all eight EXIF-JPEG orientations are decoded and re-encoded through the real adapter; the PNG fixture also carries varied alpha. Corrupt/truncated inputs are rejected. Browser imports PNG, TIFF, ICO, normal JPEG, and EXIF-oriented JPEG, visibly rejects an unsupported AVIF input without replacing the current image, exercises chooser, drag/drop, and multi-image clipboard import, protects text-field paste, and compares generated output bytes with the rendered canvas. Color-profile behavior remains a fixture boundary. |
| Input safety and mixed sets | A + B/M | Fast checks detect animated GIF/WebP, enforce decoded-pixel limits, stable fingerprints, and duplicate identity; browser imports a mixed PNG/animated-GIF set and keeps the valid preview while showing an actionable error for the animated item. |
| Pan, zoom, fit-to-screen | B/M | Zoom and Fit screen controls are automated; browser smoke performs a real Space-drag pan and asserts the canvas pixels move, dispatches a two-pointer pinch and double-tap fit-to-screen, and covers keyboard +/−/F navigation plus keyboard crop movement. A real-device touch/accessibility matrix remains a follow-on boundary. |
| Stale-download prevention and generated preview | B/M | Browser delays the worker, changes the size, asserts Download is disabled while the old result is invalidated, then decodes the actual generated PNG blob and compares every rendered canvas channel for 4×4 fit, direct 8×6 crop, advanced 4×4 crop, and a compound rotate/flip/adjust result before comparing Original and Edited snapshots. Broader input/color-profile parity remains a fixture-roadmap item. |
| Space-drag pan and visible keyboard shortcuts | B/M | Source wiring and live editor controls expose Space pan, +/−, F, C, Enter, Escape, undo, and Download shortcuts; browser smoke performs the Space-drag and covers the keyboard alternatives. |
| Crop presets and handles | A + B/M | Real crop dimensions and varied-alpha crop pixels are asserted; browser selects and shape-checks Original, Square, 4:3, 3:4, 16:9, and 9:16, applies a real 16:9 preset and compares its generated bytes with the canvas, performs a real pointer drag on a crop handle, uses Enter to apply plus arrow-key nudging with Escape cancel, then applies a manual crop. |
| Mixed-shape crop framing review | A + B/M | The framing helper detects source-shape differences when a shared crop destination can remove content; fast checks identify the flagged item, while browser smoke applies Square to square and portrait sources, shows a plain-language Review framing notice, marks the tray/card, verifies the flagged card, removes it, and confirms the notice clears. Keep whole image does not raise the warning. |
| Fit resize and exact Crop resize | A + B | Real 4×4 fit and exact crop output dimensions; browser deliberately opens Size, verifies locked and unlocked width/height behavior, changes Advanced sizing and both modes, then verifies the generated preview. |
| Rotate and flip | A + B | Real rotated dimensions and changed flip bytes; browser invokes the controls. |
| Brightness, contrast, grayscale | A + B | Real adjusted PNG bytes differ; browser drives the controls, checks signed percentage labels (`+25%`, `+20%`), and resets brightness to `0`. |
| Text layers and local fonts | A + B/M | Browser UI checks text editing, dirty state, canvas parity and Reset. The shared compositor has exact PNG/JPEG checks across the direct engine, 1/4/8 workers and journaled folder files, with a pinned OFL Noto Sans fixture, real FontFace decoding, alpha, grayscale plus colored text, missing/corrupt/oversized font failure and active-font retention after cleanup. System fonts vary by device; the story pack is covered separately below, while full script shaping and physical browsers remain open. See [evidence](docs/TEXT_COMPOSITOR_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Undo, redo, Reset, dirty state | B/M | Browser transition sequence asserts dirty visibility and history behavior. |
| Destination presets and scope | A + B/M | Preset names/dimensions are data-tested; browser selects outcome-named quick choices, opens More destinations, uses Website Banner in the tray, and exercises explicit All/Selected/This scope with per-item destination markers. The no-resize utility is named `Edit without resizing` and is not a primary destination. |
| Custom save/edit/duplicate/delete | B/M | Browser saves a named canvas recipe with final format and capability-gated lossy choice, verifies the stored recipe, applies that complete recipe into the active tray, exercises real JPEG edits and a deliberately overclaimed AVIF format to verify honest failures, restores the original shared destination, duplicates it, and deletes both local copies. |
| Batch limits and cancellation | A + B | Worker revision/cancel protocol, explicit Cancel updates behavior, and the 40-file interactive-preview limit are contract-tested. Before selection, browsers without writable-folder access label the fallback `Choose folder (up to 40)`. Browser smoke rejects 41 files with the memory-safety reason and the supported large-folder route, cancels from Results and the editor tray, then retries the cancelled cards to completion. |
| One-or-more image workflow | A + B/M | The same adapter, recipe, output settings, and save paths serve one image or many. A multi-file import stays in the canvas workspace; the tray applies a destination or current canvas changes to All, Selected, or This image; one result saves directly. Several use one uniquely named folder where writable-folder access exists, or an explicit one-click-per-file queue in other browsers. At 320px and 390px, the tray keeps its Save selected action in-bounds. |
| Unified active-set results drawer | B/M | With an active canvas image, `Results (N)` opens the result-first drawer while the editor remains the underlying workspace; `Back to editor` returns to the same canvas, Presets closes the drawer before opening, and clearing the last result returns automatically. There is no separate batch/single mode switch. |
| Batch preview grid | B/M | Browser waits for completed result-first cards, output dimensions, and verifies the original stays hidden until the press/release comparison action is held. |
| Add more images to an active image set | B/M | Browser appends a second fixture without removing the first, preserves the compact drop area, and keeps completed items selected. |
| Re-import the same file, Remove image, New set, Retry, and Clear completed | A + B/M | Source checks expose bounded recovery paths; browser smoke exercises append/remove, cancellation followed by Retry, Clear completed, and confirmed New set. Clear completed removes only ready previews. |
| Selection and Select all | B/M | Completed results are selected by default; browser clears, reselects, and checks Save enablement. |
| Individual and selected save | A + B | PNG signatures are real-byte tested; browser compares direct and per-image-override save bytes with generated previews. With writable-folder access, several selected outputs are written to one uniquely named browser-managed folder, read back, decoded, and checked to contain no archive. With folder access disabled, browser smoke proves the initial action launches zero downloads, the dialog contains no preview, every explicit click launches exactly one real PNG, filenames stay unique and ordered, and completion says downloads started rather than claiming disk writes. |
| Download sheet | A + B/M | The browser checks the metadata-only sheet for a capability with multiple choices, verifies dimensions/file size/format and no second image preview, then validates direct PNG bytes when a single-format capability is injected. |
| Single-image Download route | A + B | Fast checks validate generated PNG bytes; browser asserts the top-bar Download path and the absence of a duplicate preview. One and many images use the same selection/configuration model. |
| Keyboard shortcuts and ownership | B/M | Browser exercises unmodified Fit/Crop/zoom, Cmd/Ctrl+Z and redo, text-entry isolation, and Cmd/Ctrl+S. Results owns its save shortcut exclusively and invokes exactly one selected folder save; editor shortcuts yield to Results, Presets, open dialogs, browser Find/Copy, and native text-field undo. |
| Apply current edits and per-item override merge | A + B/M | Fast checks prove relative crop scaling, shared-edit merging, removal of only the applied override keys, and preservation of unrelated per-image corrections. Browser rotates one image, applies that change to all, opens another image to verify the shared rotation, then adds a local flip and confirms later destination/format changes do not silently replace it. |
| Active-set refresh recovery | A + B/M | Fast checks validate the versioned source-byte snapshot schema, shared override, quality, recipe scope, per-item destination, and override metadata. Browser proves one-image and multi-image restoration opens the canvas only after true source dimensions are known, preventing a no-resize recipe from becoming 1×1; generated outputs are rebuilt, not restored as truth. |
| Local data summary and clear | A + B/M | Fast checks cover the shared recipe key and byte formatting; browser creates a local recipe and recovery copy, opens the footer summary, verifies recipe/font/recovery counts and storage size, clears saved data with confirmation, keeps the open image usable, and refreshes without a stale recovery offer. Custom-font decoding and active-edit font retention have an isolated real-font browser check. |
| Hold-to-compare | B/M | Browser dispatches pointer down/up on the editor comparison control and asserts Original is active only while held; image-set cards expose the same press-to-see-original pattern. |
| Private/offline processing | B/M | The compound browser journey records every request and fails if any request has a body or leaves the local test origin; in-memory `blob:` preview URLs are explicitly allowed. Run `fb944f00-936b-481c-9fc7-c4b2e7829426` passed this check. This proves the current app flow does not upload image bytes, not that a future deployment can never add a third-party asset. |
| No console errors | B | Headless smoke collects console/page errors across the compound journey; run `fb944f00-936b-481c-9fc7-c4b2e7829426` passed with no console/page errors. |
| Responsive control layout and stable editor chrome | B/M | Browser smoke measures visible header, Add images/Results actions, recipe/output controls, the five primary tools, and selection controls at 320/375/390/768/1024/1440px widths. It also compares header height and workspace position across clean, dirty, processing, and ready states and requires Download to remain visible-but-disabled while output is stale. Results imports a long filename, opens destination/card menus, exercises a capability-gated multi-format state, checks 200% text size at 390px, and hit-tests then clicks a mobile card menu. It fails on overlap, clipped text, viewport escape, hidden controls leaking into the UI, targets below 44px on phones, or page overflow. |
| Truthful capability-driven formats | A + B/M | File pickers and drag/drop follow the runtime input list; output choices follow runtime encoder support, and unsupported files/formats get actionable messages. Format remains discoverable even when only PNG is verified, while unavailable formats and quality controls are not faked. Emitted bytes must pass signature and decode/dimension checks. |
| Format conversion and lossy compression | A + B/M | The fast suite renders real PNG/JPEG through the pinned published binding, checks opaque/partial/transparent JPEG backgrounds, proves stale quality values cannot become extension hints, and rejects PNG masquerading as JPEG. Browser-native decoding checks actual PNG/JPEG pixels independently. The published runtime exposes no quality setting, so its controls stay hidden. Synthetic future-capability tests retain quality-state and preset-round-trip coverage; overclaimed AVIF must fail and disable Download. |
| Shared output settings across one and many images | A + B/M | Canvas, tray, Results, and saved recipes use the same verified format/lossy/quality state. Fast checks enforce Low=80, Medium=95 (default), High=100; browser verifies each choice and that format/quality values survive preset and per-image merges. |
| Destination preset semantics | A + B/M | Fast data checks cover exact dimensions/mode; browser selects a named destination in the editor, saves it through the visual preset dialog, checks the stored dimensions, and reuses named destinations in both tray and review surfaces. |
| Output and import safety limits | A + B/M | Fast checks reject oversized requested output before allocation, preserve still GIFs containing comma bytes in comments, reject valid multi-frame GIFs, enforce the shared pixel budget, and test exact batch-byte-limit acceptance versus one-byte-over rejection; batch preflights total input bytes before reading candidates. Browser covers the user-facing 40-file bound and actionable oversized/animated outcomes. |
| Shared parallel processing | A + B/M | 38 scheduler checks cover combined CPU/memory admission, deferred copies, priorities/aging, lifecycle, cancellation/failure, Auto/cooldown, mixed-image calibration, header-only work, idle gaps and initial cohorts that follow useful arrivals. Downward trials challenge an unmeasured initial guess, compare the same work family and restore the measured baseline when an incomplete trial drains. Missing/small resource hints and short jobs keep a serial start; memory/output and pressure safeguards remain. Historical evidence is retained. Source/packaged Chromium preserves exact 1/2/4/8 outputs and origin admission. The [startup calibration record](docs/research/2026-09-20/auto-calibration/README.md) separates modeled policy checks from browser timing; [physical-device and memory qualification](docs/SHARED_SCHEDULER_VERIFICATION.md) remains open. |
| Browser collection throughput | B | Auto startup calibration run `benchmark-6a30d31a-8f7b-40c1-8cd8-0c3d63aed3d7`: 100 measured jobs / 3,600 images; 174 jobs / 6,264 checked outputs including gates/warmups. All output and final source/raw-statistic checks passed. Five randomized repetitions include source scan, normal validation and journaled OPFS writes. All four Auto blocks meet the 1.10 timing comparison against every eligible fixed setting. Budgets: 16 pass, 1 fail, 4 not proven; fixed 16 exceeds this host's budget. The retained tiny-PNG failure and earlier matrices remain visible. Dirty target, physical phone, complete memory/UI and heavy scene qualification remain open. [Method, reports and receipt](docs/COLLECTION_BENCHMARKS.md#auto-startup-calibration-matrix-20-september-2026). |
| Native HEIC capability research | B (research) | Two generated 256 × 192 inputs run through bitmaps, image elements and workers. Playwright WebKit 26.5 decodes with correct dimensions and alpha; Chromium 151 rejects them. Raw color differences, input/runtime hashes and unsuccessful sandbox encoder attempts are retained. This is not application HEIC support, independent color/decoder quality or physical-phone evidence. [Probe and boundaries](docs/research/2026-09-17/heic-native-spike/README.md). |
| 100,000-file metadata contract | A + B/M | Fast checks construct 100,000 manifest records without source/output byte fields and bound visible rows. Folder reads/renders/writes use the shared scheduler; source dimensions are inspected before render admission and results stay worker-local through the completed write. Browser smoke checks pause returns queued claims to pending, resume and repaired-source retry, and real transformed output files. Advertised-scale physical memory and filesystem qualification remain open. |
| Folder ownership and interrupted writes | B/M | `npm run verify:folder-recovery` uses real IndexedDB, OPFS, Web Locks and terminated workers for two-tab exclusion, stale-owner/attempt fencing, 24 concurrent writes, duplicate-safe counters, recovery during write and after close, retry-only-failed, changed-output protection and unsupported-exclusive-mode failure. Full UI checks competing-tab controls. Native folders, OS/process crashes and power-loss behavior remain physical release gates. See [evidence](docs/FOLDER_RECOVERY_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Folder rendering identity and font snapshots | A + B/M | Five model checks and real IndexedDB/OPFS/Pillow tests cover recipe/renderer identity, atomic private font capture, simultaneous/stale preparation, reload after library removal, corrupt/missing assets, ignored unbound font descriptors, authoritative saved destinations, blocked database upgrade and preserved legacy outputs. 49 successful outputs match serial at observed peaks 1/4/8, with two expected asset failures. This proves these correctness cases, not throughput or physical-device behavior; see [evidence](docs/FOLDER_RENDER_CONTRACT_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Multiple-shape story exports | A + B/M | Ordered complete output counts, frozen project/format/shapes, copied output styles, legacy single-shape behavior, independent failures, retry-only-failed, pause/continue and cleanup. Real engine checks compare eight reduced-size outputs at each of 1/4/8 workers and eight full-size portrait/tall phone exports against serial hashes and native decoding. Phone UI covers saved choices, output-style application, attention filtering, downloads, activated sharing, 200% text and Back during preparation. Queue progress is local to the open sheet; physical capacity and durable grouped-story jobs remain open. [Evidence](docs/STORY_EXPORT_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Project model/history/recovery | A + B/M | Fifty-four model/layout/style/legacy-migration/catalog/selection tests cover runtime hashes, exact PNG/JPEG serialization, legacy geometry, bounded undo/redo, scoped/variant override precedence, connected coordinates, validation, scene placement, story assembly, reversible style/reflow changes, catalog mutation fences and revision-specific selections. Real IndexedDB tests cover separated assets, legacy preservation, renderer archives, atomic saves, revision fences and backup. Story checks include exact rendered reload, lazy reads, competing tabs, conflict-copy UI and retained open assets after collection. Archive import and physical storage remain open; see [evidence](docs/PROJECT_MODEL_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Multi-photo scene API | A + B/M | Real Pillow/OffscreenCanvas checks cover ordering, fitting/crops/rotation, alpha/grayscale, masks and text occlusion, EXIF, connected seams, group opacity, asset integrity, exact preview downsampling and PNG/JPEG export. Twelve outputs at each of 1/4/8 workers match with frozen revisions and cancellation/admission checks. Source and packaged Chromium run the same suite. Model inference and throughput qualification remain open; see [evidence](docs/SCENE_COMPOSITOR_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Mobile story workspace | A + B/M | Six-photo/four-slide touch workflow checks crop/source reflow, per-shape positions, keep/reset/warnings, own-photo look thumbnails, one-step undo/cancel, output variants, browser Back, 200% text, exact reload, two-tab conflict copies, local-data cleanup, ordered independently decoded 1080×1920 JPEGs and an actual download. Sharing uses a test double to check ordered File objects and fresh user activation; physical destinations remain untested. Light/dark screenshots are visually checked. Authored catalog qualification, representative real-photo layout review and actual phones remain open; see [evidence](docs/STORY_WORKSPACE_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Manual cutout editing and source-pixel detail | A + B/M | Real mask import/soft brushes, source alpha, local/story undo, cancel, exact recovery, quota retry and source replacement. Independent browser decoding checks exact original pixels in bounded detail crops; 100/200/400% UI, one-pixel pointer/keyboard edits, pan/zoom history preservation, worker failure/retry, resizing and deferred-read cancellation are exercised. Saved full masks contain only the intended changed pixels. Automatic segmentation and representative photographic edge/device qualification remain open; see [evidence](docs/MASK_EDITING_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Manual depth titles | A + B/M | Independent alpha-composition oracle, one source/mask decode, crop/rotation/opacity/look checks, exact preview and 1/2/4/8-worker output identity. Phone controls, Cutout handoff, 200% text, Cancel/Undo/Redo, quota retry, exact saved recovery and ordered PNG exports are exercised. Mask/source changes retain the title with a visible front-text fallback; a new mask restores depth and corrupt masks fail explicitly. Depth cover quality qualification, automatic subjects, real-photo quality and physical devices remain open; see [evidence](docs/DEPTH_TITLE_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Connected cutouts | A + B/M | Shared adjacent-pair nodes, independent copies/mask ownership, per-shape positions, depth-title transfer, grouped slide/chain reordering and strict one-sided-override rejection. Browser checks require independently decoded spread references, exact pixels after reorder, 1/2/4/8-worker identity, phone controls, Back/undo/reload and ordered exports matched to saved-document renders. Real-photo edge/seam quality, physical devices and throughput remain open; see [evidence](docs/CONNECTED_CUTOUT_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Adaptive layouts | A + B/M | Counts 6–12, varied aspects, rotated bounds/borders, row-to-stack reflow, crop rounding, overrides and old-story opt-in are checked. Both variant PNGs match a flattened plain reference graph with equivalent physical type sizes. Geometry is not a perceptual quality or semantic-subject guarantee; see [evidence](docs/ADAPTIVE_LAYOUT_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Story style library | A + B/M | Saved/Recent/favorites, selected-field capture, safe file roundtrip, copied revisions, one-step undo, scoped corrections and unavailable requirements have mobile/browser evidence. Real two-tab IndexedDB checks cover conflicts, quotas, bounded capacity, pending-save cleanup and unknown-data backup. Eighteen-style browsing checks lazy previews and 200% text. The bundled story font pack is covered below; full story-style per-image/bulk consumers and physical performance remain open; see [evidence](docs/STYLE_LIBRARY_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Legacy preset migration | A + B/M | Original recipe JSON is retained; copied revisions preserve IDs, metadata and transform order. Three-aspect actual-render comparisons are byte-identical for original, migrated and folder settings. Browser checks explicit unsupported-output replacement, editor/recovery copies, concurrent revision allocation, quota/reopen retry and clearing. Story-style bulk execution, first-generation sessions without copied definitions and physical scale remain open; see [evidence](docs/LEGACY_PRESET_MIGRATION.md). |
| Transactional recipe catalog | A + B/M | Two-tab creates merge; stale edits/deletes fail without partial writes. Drafts survive with a save-copy action; applied project definitions survive remote deletion. Quota rollback, idempotent retry after committed-but-unreadable saves, cross-tab clear generation, schema upgrades, future/malformed-data fences, atomic catalog/definition backups and newer-database clear refusal pass. Phone-width and 200% text checks cover recovery; physical device qualification remains open. [Evidence](docs/LEGACY_PRESET_MIGRATION.md). |
| Revision-specific bulk choices | A + B/M | Different images can retain two revisions of one ID. Real browser output hashes verify this-image/selected changes, manual correction preservation, exact reload after library removal, and stable folder labels and actual worker output. Recovery v2 rejects missing or inconsistent references and archives an earlier v1 record. The actual phone Batch sheet fits at 375×667 and 200% text. [Evidence and historical-recovery limits](docs/RECIPE_SELECTION_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Large-folder discovery, direct output, pause/retry, and recovery | A + B/M | Start stays unavailable until metadata discovery is complete. Browser smoke chooses source/output directories, pauses and resumes pending work, creates a real failed input, proves the failed terminal state shows only `Retry N failed` rather than an ineffective Resume, repairs and retries it, reads direct results back, checks PNG signatures/dimensions, proves no archive exists, bounds result DOM rows, and reloads a saved discovered job. Interrupted processing entries reset to pending; interrupted discovery is cleared and restarted from the durable source handle. Browser permission can still require a person to approve access again after restart. |
| Contextual inspector and mobile controls sheets | B/M | Browser checks native More/Batch/tool dialogs, focus return and Escape, navigation to Presets, grayscale edit preservation across closing and desktop resizing, six visible tools, reachable batch save and hidden unsupported quality controls. The 375×667 check requires a canvas occupying at least 55% of the screen and an on-screen tool dock. Editor/Results text scaling, reduced-motion, forced-colors, and high-contrast emulation also run. Physical keyboard, platform Back, landscape, touch and accessibility validation remain open; see [phone shell evidence](docs/MOBILE_SHELL_VERIFICATION.md). |
| Accessible canvas state | A + B/M | Source checks require a dynamic canvas label; browser smoke verifies it names the current image, output size, and Keep whole image behavior. Keyboard crop movement, Enter/Escape, focus-visible styling, reduced-motion, forced-colors, and high-contrast emulation are covered. Screen-reader, real touch, RTL, and 200% text-zoom validation remain open. |
| Contributor command and CI contract | A + CI | The fast contract checks the Make targets, npm gate, Pages assembly/checker, and current workflow action versions. `make package-pages` builds the exact allowlisted artifact, minifies app-owned JS/CSS, preserves the published JS/WASM pair unchanged, emits Brotli sidecars, validates JavaScript syntax, and round-trips every sidecar back to its source bytes. CI checks npm signatures/provenance and exact migration comparisons; a hosted Actions run and the Pages host's actual transfer headers remain deployment-system boundaries. |
| Release asset optimization | A + B/M + CI | The artifact checker proves non-empty minified assets, valid WASM, byte-identical Brotli decompression, and a valid packaged browser artifact. The browser smoke serves `_site` with `TINY_IMAGE_STAR_BROWSER_ROOT=_site` in the Pages build job, so the minified modules and Brotli WASM path are exercised before upload. Identifier minification is only a size optimization, not security obfuscation. |
| Documentation navigation | A | `npm run check:docs` scans repository Markdown and rejects missing local link targets. External URL availability, anchor semantics, and rendered publication layout remain manual/release-review boundaries. |

## Authored story recipe verification

The [three authored story recipes](docs/STORY_RECIPE_VERIFICATION.md) have
distinct cover/body/closing roles, framing, type and attached decorations.
Nine model tests cover counts 6–12, both shapes, independent attachment geometry,
crop/mask/word preservation, cover-mask preflight, filled layout styles, recipe
replacement, immutable definitions and undo. The browser workflow checks new
story defaults, actual own-photo previews/downloads, 200% text, saved recovery,
18 real-photo renders and ordered export. Eight slide jobs match live serial
output at observed worker peaks 1, 4 and 8 without admission violations.
Representative font/quality review, grouped/bulk composition,
automatic subjects, sustained performance and physical devices remain open.

## Bundled story font verification

[Recipe revision two](docs/STORY_FONT_VERIFICATION.md) adds four pinned OFL
fonts with original licenses and source metadata. Seven model tests cover
hashes, complete independent cmap comparison, immutable revision-one behavior,
safe references, glyph/face preflight, fallback/undo and bounded cancellable
loading. The phone browser workflow covers real variable faces, actual style
downloads, failed/cancelled loads, saved-font reload with font requests blocked,
unsupported text, explicit fallback, 44px font controls and 200% text. This does
not establish whole-app offline availability, full shaping support, physical
phone behavior or complete font-cache memory accounting.

## Explicit smaller story sources

[Working-copy import](docs/WORKING_COPY_VERIFICATION.md) retains originals and
uses reduced sources only after explicit consent. Five model tests cover
lineage, default/small-source byte preservation, full-decode admission, output
ownership and cancellation. The focused browser workflow covers a real 12MP
source, independent EXIF coordinate mappings, alpha, observed 1/4/8-worker
identity, saved originals, exact reload, source switching and undo. Default
depth/outline/shadow fits the tested 512 MiB admission case; maximum effects are
still rejected before source reads. Physical memory, representative crop
quality and general camera/color support remain separate gates.

Existing-story source conversion adds seven model regressions and a real-engine
phone workflow. It preserves connected geometry, crops, text and current masks,
restores untouched originals exactly, resizes painted masks with an explicit
detail warning, and supports atomic Apply/Cancel/undo/reload. Source-copy jobs
produce identical results at observed 1/4/8-worker peaks; failure, cancellation,
photo selection and retry preserve the current document. References share the
declared Pillow Lanczos resampler and use independent browser PNG decoding.
See [scope and retained evidence](docs/WORKING_COPY_VERIFICATION.md#existing-edited-photos-reversible-resolution).

## Cutout finish verification

Reusable depth-title styles have five additional model regressions and an
extended mobile browser workflow: private words/masks are excluded from the
actual style download; existing words, crops and masks survive; keep/reset
position, connected scope, one-step undo and exact reload/export are checked.
See the [depth-style record](docs/STYLE_LIBRARY_VERIFICATION.md#depth-style-addition-20-september-2026).
The authored recipe implementation is described above; bulk depth composition,
catalog qualification and physical devices remain open.

Story cutout outlines and shadows are covered separately in
[cutout finish verification](docs/CUTOUT_EFFECTS_VERIFICATION.md): independent
soft-mask morphology and alpha expectations, padded scene admission, connected
seams/depth composition, grouped history and reusable finish styles. This is
manual/imported-mask functionality; the model research below does not enable
automatic selection.

## Scene materialization verification

Scene resource work also has [explicit materialization evidence](docs/SCENE_MATERIALIZATION_VERIFICATION.md):
twelve original/viewport pairs and four depth-source pairs retain exact PNG
hashes for synthetic 3 MP/12 MP PNG and JPEG inputs. Binding traces explain
repeated transform work; mixed Wasm-memory results remain visible. Instrumented
single-desktop timings do not qualify sustained throughput or phone capacity.

## Automatic-selection research boundary

The [segmentation spike](docs/SEGMENTATION_RESEARCH.md) pins SDK/model/photo
inputs and records a ten-case local Chromium matrix: nine successful three-image
mask runs and one retained no-WebGL CPU failure. It includes actual cutout
inspection, SDK telemetry attempts, successful enforced worker/header and
document/blob CSP probes, offline hash checks and a fresh-cache reproduction.
This research is excluded from the Pages artifact and does not add automatic
selection to the app. Three small photos, software SwiftShader and sampled Wasm
allocations do not qualify representative quality, mobile memory, GPU speed,
large-collection throughput or the complete privacy/license release gate.

## Known automation boundary

The browser download event may be suppressed by a browser sandbox even after
the app has generated the correct single-file bytes and invoked the save
anchor. The fast test validates those bytes directly, while browser smoke also
exercises real download events for the explicit multi-file fallback. Multi-image
direct-folder and large-folder saves are additionally written into browser-managed directories,
then read back and decoded by the browser smoke. A native operating-system
folder picker and permission re-prompt still require real-browser/manual release
QA because headless automation replaces only that picker boundary.
No feature is marked passed solely because a label appeared in the DOM.
